"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"I started by defining the user pain points, brainstorming core features, and designing a clean UI in PowerPoint to make the functionality feel simple and accessible."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg","children":"Technical Implementation"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"I built the data analysis pipeline using Pandas and PyPDF2. To enable the core features, I implemented:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"!my-4","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"MD5 Hashing"}]," for efficient duplicate detection."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"TF-IDF & Cosine Similarity"}]," to engineer a content-based search engine with Scikit-learn."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"K-Means Clustering"}]," to automatically group similar documents based on their content vectors."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"OCR Integration"}]," with Pytesseract to extract text from scanned PDFs."]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold !mb-6","children":"3. The Solution: DocuSense in Action"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The result is a practical PDF management tool built on a foundation of data science. The prototype delivers three core features:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mt-8 text-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col items-center","children":[["$","$L15",null,{"src":"/projects/docusense/feature-dashboard.png","alt":"DocuSense Dashboard","width":300,"height":600,"className":"rounded-2xl"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-semibold mt-4","children":"Analytics Dashboard"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":"Instant insights on your entire PDF collection."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col items-center","children":[["$","$L15",